WEBVTT

NOTE Visual description and on-screen text; not spoken narration.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
White words appear on a dark background.
On-screen text: A doctor is close on the map. Out of reach in practice.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
The words appear as a list; “A doctor” is crossed out before the final sentence appears.
On-screen text: Rent. Food. A ride. A doctor. When money is tight, care waits.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
A large population figure appears with its definition and source date.
On-screen text: 5.29 million. People in designated primary-care shortage areas in New York. This is not a count of people without care. HRSA · September 30, 2026 · Exact reported population: 5,288,766.

4
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:28.500
Two horizontal bars share a 0–100% scale, marked at 0%, 25%, 50%, 75% and 100%. The New York bar is shorter than the national-total bar.
On-screen text: Primary-care workforce need met. In designated primary-care shortage areas. New York: 35.42%. National total: 46.75%. New York: 11.33 percentage points below the national total. HRSA, FY2026 Q4, Table 3 · September 30, 2026. National total includes New York. Workforce measure, not appointment access.

5
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.000
A line connects the words “HOME” and “CARE” on a blue background.
On-screen text: What if care came within reach? HOME. CARE.

6
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.500
Four supports appear in two columns, separated by thin blue rules.
On-screen text: Four supports. One clear route. Sponsored direct primary care membership. Ongoing telehealth. Help with transportation. Health access education. With Dr. Michael Purcell and Purcell Integrative Osteopathic Care, a direct primary care practice in Clifton Park. Clinical care remains with the licensed provider. Membership is not health insurance.

7
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.000
Three large blue figures—“Up to 25,” “12” and “2027”—appear above the supporting text.
On-screen text: The first cohort. Up to 25 New Yorkers aged 64 or younger. 12 months of support per participant. 2027, beginning in January. One per household · Financial need · A chronic condition. Any of New York’s 62 counties.

8
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.000
The funding, reporting and clinical boundaries appear as large text on white.
On-screen text: Funds confirmed before enrollment. Reports at months 3, 6, 9 and 12. Clinical care stays with the licensed provider. Sponsors do not select participants or influence clinical care.

9
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The budget is displayed in large white type on blue; it is a planned budget, not a fundraising progress counter.
On-screen text: First-cohort budget. $108,000. About $4,320 per participant for a full year. Sponsorships from $5,000 · Other amounts welcome.

10
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
The SozoRock wordmark and sponsor invitation close the video.
On-screen text: SozoRock. Care within reach. Become a sponsor — sozorockfoundation.org. Care. For every ZIP Code. The SozoRock Foundation, Inc., a 501(c)(3) public charity.

